  "about": "Santiago bank/LBTR closures (Banco Central de Chile LBTR in CLP; dólar observado). National legal holidays (Law 2.977 and amendments) plus the Dec 31 bank holiday (Ley General de Bancos art. 38: removed by the Fintec Law 21.521 but kept in practice per CMF, restored by Law 21.791 of 17 Dec 2025). Law 19.668 (2000) moves San Pedro y San Pablo, Encuentro de Dos Mundos and (to 2006) Corpus Christi: Tue-Thu to that week's Monday, Fri to the next Monday, weekend days stay; Law 20.148 replaced Corpus Christi with Jul 16 from 2007; Law 20.299 adds Oct 31 from 2008 (Tue->previous Fri, Wed->next Fri); Laws 20.215 and 20.983 add Sep 17/Sep 20 and Jan 2 bridge days; Law 21.357 adds the solstice indigenous day from 2021. Moving holidays are given as computed date tables. Checked against the 2026 published list (24horas) and the 2024 list; Santiago-only 2018-01-16 papal-visit holiday included. Elections are Sundays (Law 20.354) and never close a weekday 2005-2026. Coverage 2005-2026; 2027 entries are rule-based only.",
